[
  {
    "_comment": "CDC scenario QUIET TABLE: Db2 CDC over the ASN SQL-Replication CD tables the db2cdc system registers for every model table, asncap copying each change a moment after it commits; column names arrive upper-cased and are matched without case. The CD tables carry the rows an ON DELETE CASCADE takes but not an UPDATE that changes nothing: --cascades logged --noops unlogged. Db2 has no snapshot isolation, so an initial load under changes may load a change and replay it too. `readings` is tracked and left alone for 3 rollovers, then changed: a slot that carried nothing for several versions must still carry its table's changes, and the tables around it every one of theirs. STAGES: (1) domains -- create the db2cdc domain, install employeescdc, load the xs seed; (2) actions -- `sentinel-data --key after-create-data`; (3) collections and (4) functions -- register db2cdc_initial_load (initial_load=True); (5) sentinel -- the load has flushed; then 3 times: actions -- `modify-data --entity accounts,ledger,devices,audit --ops Mix --sets 6` and `sentinel-data --key quiet-<n>`, and a sentinel stage holding until quiet-<n> arrives, so each pass is published in a version of its own before the next starts -- a rollover with nothing for readings; after the second pass a 75s pause, past the publisher's 1-minute fallback window, with nothing changing at all; then actions -- `modify-data --entity readings --ops Mix --sets 6`, one more `modify-data --ops Mix --sets 6` over every table, `sentinel-data --key after-changes`; a sentinel; actions, tagged check -- scripts/verify_cdc_ops.py --start initial-load: every change one by one in its transaction, nothing of audit; monitor. Generated by gen_suites.py. Run: `tdd xp one-shot --suite cdc/db2cdc_quiet_table --keep`."
  },
